Subject: [PATCH] fonts: a Windows persona answers Helvetica on a Windows host

Stock Chrome on Windows shows Helvetica, measuring as Arial. A Windows
persona hid it on a Windows host, because patch 0146 answered the names
Windows aliases through the alternate family only on Linux. Windows has
no Helvetica face, so its own lookup answers Helvetica with Arial, as
stock Chrome's does. A Mac host still hides these names, since its lookup
would reach the Mac's own Helvetica.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
index 631753e..fe12421 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
@@ -227,10 +227,11 @@ bool FontCache::ProfileHidesFamily(const AtomicString& family) {
   // way Windows does (CreateWindowsPersonaTypeface in skia/font_cache_skia.cc):
   // a name no face answers to falls back to its alternate family (Helvetica
   // is Arial), and a name Windows files a listed family under finds that
-  // family (Franklin Gothic is Franklin Gothic Medium). Other builds keep
-  // these names hidden, because their lookup would reach the host's own
+  // family (Franklin Gothic is Franklin Gothic Medium). A Windows host answers
+  // them that way itself, as stock Windows Chrome shows Helvetica. A Mac host
+  // keeps these names hidden, because its lookup would reach the host's own
   // Helvetica.
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
   const bool windows_names = ClaimsWindows(*profile);
 #else
   const bool windows_names = false;
